<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Detection reads foreground-window titles via CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo,
       which requires the Screen Recording permission (System Settings →
       Privacy & Security → Screen Recording). macOS shows its own prompt on
       first use; these strings document intent for users and App Review. -->
  <key>NSScreenCaptureUsageDescription</key>
  <string>StatusForge reads the title of the active game window to detect what you are playing. No screen content is recorded.</string>
  <key>NSAccessibilityUsageDescription</key>
  <string>StatusForge inspects window metadata to detect the active game.</string>
  <!-- The LAN Hub (SPARK Dual-PC Link) broadcasts on udp/53736 and listens
       for SPARK heartbeats on udp/53735 — macOS gates any local-subnet
       traffic behind the Local Network permission (Sequoia 15+) separately
       from Screen Recording above; without this key macOS silently drops
       the traffic or endlessly re-prompts instead of asking once. -->
  <key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
  <string>StatusForge's LAN Hub listens on your local network for a paired SPARK agent on a second PC, so it can mirror game detections between the two machines.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
